\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Primaries in Southern States Will Be Barometer for G.O.P.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Maya King \par \uc2 1,469 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 May 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 14\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Alabama, Arkansas and Texas are also holding primaries and runoff elections that will offer new hints of where voters stand on national issues and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's standing in the Republican Party.\par \par \uc2 The country's political focus will shift to the South on Tuesday with elections in Georgia, Alabama, Arkansas and Texas that will signal voters' views on national issues and the strength of former President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 's endorsement power.\par \par \uc2 In Georgia, Gov. Brian Kemp appears to be easily fending off a challenge from former Senator \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  in the Republican primary for governor, which would set up a rematch with \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , the presumptive Democratic nominee. Mr. Trump recruited Mr. Perdue to run after Mr. Kemp refused to help overturn the state's 2020 presidential election results. A Trump-backed challenger is also trying to oust the state's Republican secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 In Alabama, a competitive Republican primary for Senate is unfolding after Representative Mo Brooks lost Mr. Trump's endorsement in the race in March. The election could head to a runoff.\par \par \uc2 In Texas, voters will decide runoff races for attorney general and a House seat in the Rio Grande Valley. The congressional race will pit Representative \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2 , an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Democrat who remains part of an F.B.I. investigation, against Jessica Cisneros, a progressive challenger.\par \par \uc2 And in Arkansas, \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 , Mr. Trump's former press secretary, is expected to win the Republican primary for governor.\par \par \uc2 Here are a few of the themes we'll be following on Tuesday:\par \par \uc2 In Georgia, Trump's 'big lie' will be tested.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump put Georgia at the center of his crusade against what he has falsely claimed was a ''stolen'' election. But his influence on the state's politics has appeared to wane.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Perdue, a former Kemp ally, has made challenging the results of the 2020 election the focal point of his campaign. He opened all three debates against Mr. Kemp by falsely arguing that he and Mr. Trump were victims of fraud in Georgia's presidential election and its Senate runoff races in early 2021.\par \par \uc2 Yet Georgia Republicans have gravitated toward issues beyond the last election, focusing on the state's economy, education and rising crime rates in Georgia cities. Partly as a result, Mr. Kemp has outpaced Mr. Perdue by more than 30 percentage points in recent polling and has surpassed the former senator in fund-raising by nearly $10 million.\par \par \uc2 The only other race in which the 2020 election -- and Mr. Trump's influence -- is as prominent is the contest for secretary of state. The Republican incumbent, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , is fending off a primary challenge from Representative \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2 , who has Mr. Trump's backing. Polls indicate that neither candidate has garnered more than 30 percent of support from voters, which suggests that the race is likely to go to a runoff.\par \par \uc2 Still, there are signs of life among Georgia voters: Turnout during the state's three-week early voting period topped 850,000, a large increase from the same time during the 2018 primary.\par \par \uc2 This week, Georgia will also kick off one of the country's most important Senate elections, between Senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , a Democrat running for re-election, and \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , a Republican backed by Mr. Trump who is widely expected to cruise to victory in his party's primary.\par \par \uc2 How will an Alabama Senate candidate fare after being abandoned by Trump?\par \par \uc2 Representative Mo Brooks, a longtime ally of Mr. Trump's who was involved in the effort to overturn the 2020 election results, is making a last-minute surge among conservative Alabamans that could lift him into a runoff.\par \par \uc2 But the race remains anyone's to win. An Emerson College survey of Alabama voters conducted days before the primary showed Mr. Brooks trailing two rivals: Katie Britt, a businesswoman and the former chief of staff to Senator \uc2 Richard Shelby\uc2 , who is leading the pack, and \uc2 Mike Durant\uc2 , an Army veteran.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Brooks faces headwinds at home and in Washington. Mr. Trump's move to withdraw his endorsement in March damaged the congressman's reputation among the state's Republican base.\par \par \uc2 The House committee investigating the 2021 Capitol riot has asked to interview Mr. Brooks regarding his comments about the former president's request that he ''rescind'' the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 And the congressman has made an enemy out of Senator \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the minority leader, who has poured $2 million into a super PAC opposing his campaign. Mr. McConnell supports Ms. Britt for the seat.\par \par \uc2 Outside money is playing a big role in this race, with all three top-polling contenders being aided by groups that are spending millions to slam opposing candidates and label them as out of touch with Alabama voters. One group, the pro-Durant Alabama Patriots PAC, cut a television advertisement that goes after Mr. Brooks and Ms. Britt as ''Trump-trashing, tax-raising insiders.'' Another, the Britt-supporting Alabama Christian Conservatives group, has put forth a negative advertisement targeting Mr. Durant, saying he is lenient on immigration and gun ownership.\par \par \uc2 ''Vote Katie Britt,'' the narrator says. ''She's one of us.''\par \par \uc2 In a Texas House primary, could the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue prove decisive?\par \par \uc2 Mr. Cuellar is the last anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Democrat in the House of Representatives. The leak of a draft opinion signaling that the Supreme Court is likely to overturn Roe v. Wade, the landmark \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling, this summer could make the second time the charm for Jessica Cisneros in her bid to unseat him.\par \par \uc2 The renewed fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access has underlined internal Democratic tensions as progressives line up behind Ms. Cisneros and a handful of moderates come to Mr. Cuellar's defense. On Thursday, Representative \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2 , the chair of the Congressional Progressive Caucus, endorsed Ms. Cisneros. National \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups like Emily's List have also thrown financial support behind her bid, booking television advertisements that are critical of Mr. Cuellar.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Cisneros has the backing of several other high-profile progressives in Congress, including Representative \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  and Senators Elizabeth Warren and Bernie Sanders, who have made full-throated fund-raising pitches on her behalf.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Cisneros fell short by 3.6 percentage points in her 2020 challenge to Mr. Cuellar, whom she once interned for. This time around, his campaign must contend with not only his record on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but also an F.B.I. raid of his home and campaign office in February. Mr. Cuellar has promised he did nothing wrong, and his lawyer has said that while he was cooperating with the investigation, he was not the target of it.\par \par \uc2 Texas' Democratic primary for attorney general has also placed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at its center, as both candidates pitch themselves as would-be defenders of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access against their Republican opponents, who are likely to be overwhelming favorites in November.\par \par \uc2 Rochelle Garza, a civil rights lawyer, is the front-runner in the race, having garnered more of the vote share in the primary than the other Democrat in the running, former Mayor Joe Jaworski of Galveston. Ms. Garza called the office a ''last stand'' in protecting Texans from strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 Will Texas' scandal-trailed attorney general prevail?\par \par \uc2 Mr. Cuellar is not the only candidate in Texas' runoff elections on Tuesday who has been the subject of law enforcement scrutiny for the use of his office.\par \par \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , the state's attorney general, was indicted and arrested in 2015 on still-pending charges of securities fraud. Former aides have said he violated state law by using the influence of his office to help a donor.\par \par \uc2 But he has maintained his viability in the Republican primary by pursuing a laundry list of conservative priorities, including defending an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law passed by the state last year and joining the push to criminalize transition care for transgender youths.\par \par \uc2 With the backing of Mr. Trump and relatively strong support from Texas Republicans, Mr. Paxton garnered a larger share of the vote in the March primary election than his second-round opponent, \uc2 George P. Bush\uc2 , the state's land commissioner.\par \par \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  is on track to become Arkansas's governor. What's next?\par \par \uc2 Ms. Sanders, a White House press secretary under Mr. Trump, is also political royalty in Arkansas, as the daughter of former Gov. \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Her status has put her on a glide path to the Republican nomination for governor in what is a deep-red state. It also could position her for higher political office, beyond the governor's mansion.\par \par \uc2 A Trump rally in Commerce, Ga., in March. The former president has backed candidates who push his 2020 election falsehoods. (PHOTOGRAPH BY AUDRA MELTON FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220524ei5o0005c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
