\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Archbishop Bars Pelosi From Rite\b0\par\par\uc2 By Annie Karni and Ruth Graham \par \uc2 913 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 May 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 22\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Archbishop Salvatore J. Cordileone, who has repeatedly confronted the House speaker over her backing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, said her stance was a ''grave evil.''\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- An ultraconservative archbishop in San Francisco said on Friday that Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  of California would not be permitted to receive communion in his archdiocese because of her support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Archbishop Salvatore J. Cordileone, who has repeatedly confronted Ms. Pelosi over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said in a letter on Friday that until Ms. Pelosi was willing to ''publicly repudiate'' her position defending the ''legitimacy of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,'' she would be banned from the sacrament, a central element of Catholic worship.\par \par \uc2 ''After numerous attempts to speak with Speaker Pelosi to help her understand the grave evil she is perpetrating, the scandal she is causing'' and ''the danger to her own soul she is risking, I have determined that she is not to be admitted to Holy Communion,'' Archbishop Cordileone said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  on Friday.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Ms. Pelosi, a practicing Catholic who often mentions her faith in advocating for her progressive views, did not respond to a request for comment. In a 2008 interview with \uc2 C-SPAN\uc2 , Ms. Pelosi described herself as a ''regular communicant'' and said that if she were ever denied communion, ''that would be a severe blow to me.''\par \par \uc2 The Catholic church explicitly opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which it considers among the gravest sins. Archbishop Cordileone is an outspoken critic of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and same-sex marriage, and he has also said he did not get vaccinated for the coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Last summer, he objected after Ms. Pelosi referred to herself as a ''devout Catholic'' in a news conference during which she expressed support for efforts to allow federal funding of abortions.\par \par \uc2 ''No one can claim to be a devout Catholic and condone the killing of innocent human life, let alone have the government pay for it,'' he said in a statement at the time.\par \par \uc2 He also threw his support behind an earlier attempt to bar President Biden, the country's second Catholic president, from receiving communion because of his support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 That effort failed, after Cardinal \uc2 Wilton Gregory\uc2  of Washington said he would not bar the president from receiving communion.\par \par \uc2 Archbishop Cordileone's move aimed at Ms. Pelosi came as Democrats in Congress have been trying, and failing, to push forward legislation to guarantee \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide, after a leaked Supreme Court draft opinion suggested that the court may be on the brink of overturning the nearly 50-year-old ruling that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It was the latest sign of the growing rift within the church between conservative American bishops and the Vatican.\par \par \uc2 The Vatican has warned against denying communion to politicians supportive of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  has preached that communion ''is not the reward of saints, but the bread of sinners.''\par \par \uc2 But some leading American bishops have pushed forward anyway.\par \par \uc2 Conservative bishops have tried to depict Mr. Biden as a threat to the church, given his endorsement of policies that ''advance moral evils and threaten human life and dignity, most seriously in the areas of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , contraception, marriage and gender,'' as Archbishop Jos\u233\'00\'E9 H. Gomez of Los Angeles put it in a statement on Mr. Biden's Inauguration Day.\par \par \uc2 At a meeting last fall, bishops approved new guidance on the topic that backed away from a direct conflict with the president and high-profile Catholic Democrats like Ms. Pelosi. The document did not single out individuals, but it emphasized that bishops have a ''special responsibility'' to intervene when a congregant's prominent public actions are in conflict with church teaching.\par \par \uc2 Bishops who are seen as allies of \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  cautioned that encouraging bishops to deny communion to certain politicians would lead to a ''weaponization of the eucharist.'' But others backed the move.\par \par \uc2 ''I support Archbishop Cordileone in his courageous pastoral outreach to a member of his flock,'' Bishop James D. Conley of the Diocese of Lincoln, Neb., said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In his letter, Archbishop Cordileone also noted that Ms. Pelosi has refused to speak with him since voting for the Women's Health Protection Act, a bill to ensure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access nationwide, in September.\par \par \uc2 Growing up in Baltimore, Ms. Pelosi regularly attended Mass with her family and went to Catholic school. She has said her mother had hoped she would become a nun.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Pelosi often refers to her faith in discussing her position in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 ''I come to this as a Catholic mother of five in six years and one week, and with the joy that all that meant to us,'' she said on the House floor last year, speaking in support of the bill. ''But with the recognition that it was my husband and I -- our decision. It was our decision. And we should not, in this body or in that court, be making decisions for the women in America.''\par \par \uc2 She has criticized her church for making the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a litmus test for membership.\par \par \uc2 ''They would like to throw me out, but I'm not going, because I don't want to make their day,'' she said at an event in March.\par \par \uc2 Archbishop Salvatore J. Cordileone celebrating Easter Mass in 2020. He said Speaker Nancy Pelosi would be barred from communion until she was willing to ''publicly repudiate'' her support for \uc2  rights. (PHOTOGRAPH BY Jeff Chiu/Associated Press FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220521ei5l0003y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
