\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Democrats Warn Ban On  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  May Expand\b0\par\par\uc2 By Luke Broadwater \par \uc2 799 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 May 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 18\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The alarms came after Senator \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Republican leader, called such a ban ''possible'' if a leaked Supreme Court opinion became final and his party gained control in Washington.\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- Democrats rang alarm bells on Sunday about the likelihood that Republicans would try to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, two days after an interview was published in which Senator \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  of Kentucky, the minority leader, said a ban was ''possible'' if his party gained control in Washington.\par \par \uc2 On the Sunday talk shows and in other public statements, Democratic senators said Republicans would not stop at letting the states decide the issue, but would most likely push for federal restrictions. That made it paramount, they said, that the Democratic Party maintain control of the Senate as it tries to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law.\par \par \uc2 ''We need to make sure that every single voter understands that the Republican Party and \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  does not believe that their daughters, that their mothers, that their sisters have rights to make fundamental life and death decisions,'' Senator Kirsten Gillibrand, Democrat of New York, said on CNN's ''State of the Union.'' ''We are half-citizens under this ruling. And if this is put into law, it changes the foundation of America.''\par \par \uc2 After a leaked draft decision indicated that the Supreme Court was poised to overturn Roe v. Wade, the landmark 1973 case that established a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mr. McConnell said in an interview with USA Today that a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban was ''possible'' if that draft document became an official opinion of the court.\par \par \uc2 ''If the leaked opinion became the final opinion, legislative bodies -- not only at the state level but at the federal level -- certainly could legislate in that area,'' Mr. McConnell said when asked if a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban was ''worthy of debate.''\par \par \uc2 ''So yeah, it's possible,'' he added.\par \par \uc2 Mr. McConnell argued that the discussion about a federal ban was premature, but that it was clear that the Republican Party has long been opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Discussions are already underway among some Republican senators about pushing to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a certain number of weeks, ranging from six to 20, depending on the proposal.\par \par \uc2 ''If and when the court makes a final decision, I expect everybody will be more definitive,'' Mr. McConnell said. ''But I don't think it's much secret where Senate Republicans stand on that issue.''\par \par \uc2 A document circulated by the National Republican Senatorial Committee and obtained by Axios urged candidates to be low key about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , casting themselves as ''compassionate consensus builders'' with a post-Roe America looming as early as next month.\par \par \uc2 ''States should have the flexibility to implement reasonable restrictions,'' the document states.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , Republican of South Carolina, said on ''Fox News Sunday'' that he would push a bill to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide after 20 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 ''We're one of the seven nations in the world that allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand at 20 weeks, the fifth month in pregnancy,'' Mr. Graham said. ''Congress will continue to debate this issue.''\par \par \uc2 But Senator Amy Klobuchar, Democrat of Minnesota, said on ABC's ''This Week'' that no woman wants a Republican senator -- like Ted Cruz of Texas -- deciding whether she can have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ''Who should make this decision? Should it be a woman and her doctor or a politician? Should it be Ted Cruz making this decision or a woman and her family?''\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 , a New Hampshire Democrat who is up for re-election, blasted out a news release of Mr. McConnell's comments on Saturday evening.\par \par \uc2 ''\uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  is already making it clear that if Republicans retake the Senate majority, they will quickly move to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide and roll back reproductive freedom for women all across this country, including in New Hampshire,'' Ms. Hassan said.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , Democrat of New York and the majority leader, has set up a Wednesday vote on a bill to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law. The legislation is all but certain to be blocked by Republicans, falling short of the 60 votes needed to advance past the Senate's legislative filibuster.\par \par \uc2 It also appears to lack even the simple majority it would need to pass the 50-50 Senate, given that Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin III\uc2 , the centrist Democrat from West Virginia who opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, voted against bringing up a nearly identical measure in February and showed no signs that he had shifted his position.\par \par \uc2 Senator Kirsten Gillibrand of New York said that if the draft Supreme Court decision overturning Roe v. Wade goes into effect, ''it changes the foundation of America.'' 