\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 'Settled' or 'Barbaric'? What They've Said About Roe.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joon Yun and Jin Yu Young \par \uc2 1,076 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 12\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 In the leaked draft opinion, Justice \uc2 Samuel A. Alito Jr\uc2 . wrote the majority's decision to overturn Roe v. Wade, and four other Republican-appointed justices -- \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , \uc2 Neil M. Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett M. Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett -- voted with him in the conference held among the justices, according to Politico.\par \par \uc2 The news organization reported that Justices \uc2 Stephen G. Breyer\uc2 , \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  and Elena Kagan were working on dissents. It was not clear how Chief Justice \uc2 John G. Roberts Jr\uc2 . planned to vote.\par \par \uc2 Here is what the justices, and soon-to-be Justice \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2 , who will be sworn in when Justice Breyer retires at the end of the term, have said about Roe v. Wade:\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\par \par \uc2 Justice Alito has consistently opposed legal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As a government lawyer applying for a promotion in the Reagan administration in 1985, he wrote that he was ''particularly proud'' to have helped advance the argument that ''the Constitution does not protect a right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .''\par \par \uc2 At his confirmation hearing in 2006, Justice Alito said repeatedly that Roe was a precedent that warranted respect but declined to call it ''settled law.'' He also wrote the majority opinion in a case in 2018 that overruled a major labor decision, including a 14-page discussion of the ''factors that should be taken into account in deciding whether to overrule a past decision.''\par \par \uc2 Justice Amy Coney Barrett\par \par \uc2 Justice Barrett's record shows her committed opposition to the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In 2006, she signed a newspaper ad that supported overturning the ''barbaric legacy'' of Roe.\par \par \uc2 During her confirmation hearing in 2020, Justice Barrett said that Roe was not a ''super-precedent,'' or a decision considered so well established that it could not be overturned. ''That doesn't mean that Roe should be overruled but, descriptively, it does mean that it's not a case that everyone has accepted and doesn't call for its overruling,'' she added.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Stephen Breyer\par \par \uc2 Justice Breyer has been a longtime supporter of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. ''The case of Roe v. Wade has been the law for 21 years or more,'' he said at his confirmation hearing in 1994. ''That is the law.''\par \par \uc2 He also expressed strong disapproval over a Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law prohibiting most abortions that went into effect in September. In an interview with NPR, Mr. Breyer described the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  refusal to block the law as ''very, very, very wrong.''\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\par \par \uc2 At his hearing in 2017, Justice Gorsuch attested that Roe was precedent, and that part of the value of precedent is that it ''adds to the determinacy of law.'' However, he voted against striking down laws that would restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both Texas last year and Louisiana in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Justice Elena Kagan\par \par \uc2 Justice Kagan dissented when the Supreme Court allowed the Texas law to go into effect in September, criticizing the court's practice of deciding important issues in rushed decisions without full briefing or oral argument, which Supreme Court specialists call its ''shadow docket.''\par \par \uc2 Justice Kagan has also taken a hard line on upholding precedent, perhaps more than any other current member of the court. ''It is hard to overstate the value, in a country like ours, of stability in the law,'' she has said.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\par \par \uc2 At his confirmation hearing in 2018, Justice \uc2 Brett M. Kavanaugh\uc2  called a woman's right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ''settled law.'' He referred to court cases as ''precedent on precedent,'' and said that they could not be easily overturned.\par \par \uc2 In 2003, however, he said he did not believe that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights precedent should be considered a settled legal issue, writing, ''I am not sure that all legal scholars refer to Roe as the settled law of the land at the Supreme Court level since Court can always overrule its precedent, and three current Justices on the Court would do so.''\par \par \uc2 Justice Kavanaugh has also supported \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions with some moderation. In 2019, for example, when the court temporarily blocked a Louisiana law restricting abortions, he issued a dissent that acknowledged the key legal precedent.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice Roberts was in the majority when the court in 2007 upheld a federal law banning an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedure. When the court struck down Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in 2016, he dissented.\par \par \uc2 Although known for crafting narrow and incremental decisions, the chief justice has recently voted in favor of some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice Roberts voted to strike down a restrictive Louisiana \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in 2020. In a concurring opinion, he identified what he said was the central principle of Roe v. Wade: that women have the right to end their pregnancies before fetal viability.\par \par \uc2 In September 2021, he dissented when the court refused to block the Texas law banning most abortions after six weeks, voting with the court's three remaining liberals.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\par \par \uc2 Justice Sotomayor has been the Supreme Court's leading voice in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights since the death of Justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2 . She also filed a dissent when the court refused to block the Texas law last year.\par \par \uc2 ''The Court's order is stunning,'' she wrote. ''Presented with an application to enjoin a flagrantly unconstitutional law engineered to prohibit women from exercising their constitutional rights and evade judicial scrutiny, a majority of justices have opted to bury their heads in the sand.''\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\par \par \uc2 Justice Thomas has been a committed foe of a constitutional protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In 1992, he dissented in Planned Parenthood v. Casey, in which the majority reaffirmed the core of the Roe decision, saying Roe was ''plainly wrong'' and ''should be overruled.'' In a 2000 dissent, he wrote: ''Although a state may permit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , nothing in the Constitution dictates that a state must do so.'' In 2019, he called the decision ''notoriously incorrect.''\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\par \par \uc2 At her confirmation hearing in March, Judge \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  affirmed her stance on Roe being ''settled law'' and a precedent on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases.\par \par \uc2 She added that Roe had been relied upon, and that reliance is one of the factors the court considers when it factors when to revisit a precedent.\par \par \uc2 Judge Jackson was confirmed last month and will join the Supreme Court when Justice Breyer retires at the end of the term.\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY ERIN SCHAFF/THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220504ei5400052\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
